> This document provides a sample of the API documentation for the NexaInsight Platform. It is intended for developers who want to integrate their applications with our platform and programmatically access their data and analytics.

## NexaInsight Platform API

Welcome to the NexaInsight Platform API! Our RESTful API allows you to integrate our powerful business intelligence capabilities into your own applications. With our API, you can:

*   Programmatically manage datasets.
*   Execute queries and retrieve data.
*   Embed dashboards and visualizations.
*   Automate administrative tasks.

### Authentication

All API requests must be authenticated using an API key. You can generate an API key from your account settings in the NexaInsight Platform. The API key must be included in the `Authorization` header of your requests as a Bearer token:

`Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`

### API Endpoints

#### Datasets

*   `GET /api/v1/datasets`: Retrieve a list of all datasets in your account.
*   `POST /api/v1/datasets`: Create a new dataset.
*   `GET /api/v1/datasets/{id}`: Retrieve a specific dataset by its ID.
*   `PUT /api/v1/datasets/{id}`: Update a specific dataset.
*   `DELETE /api/v1/datasets/{id}`: Delete a specific dataset.

#### Queries

*   `POST /api/v1/queries`: Execute a query against a dataset.

**Request Body:**

```json
{
  "dataset_id": "ds_12345",
  "query": "SHOW total_revenue BY month"
}
```

**Response Body:**

```json
{
  "query_id": "qy_67890",
  "status": "completed",
  "results": [
    {"month": "2025-01-01", "total_revenue": 500000},
    {"month": "2025-02-01", "total_revenue": 600000}
  ]
}
```

### Rate Limiting

Our API is rate-limited to ensure a high level of performance for all our customers. The default rate limit is 1,000 requests per minute. If you exceed this limit, you will receive a `429 Too Many Requests` error.

### SDKs

We provide official SDKs for Python and JavaScript to make it even easier to work with our API. You can find our SDKs on GitHub.

